02:32:04  DEBUG    RAW RESPONSE:
    The role of the Chubby lock service in Bigtable is to keep track of tablet servers and manage their assignments. According to **5.2 Tablet Assignment (Pages 5-5)**, Bigtable uses Chubby to monitor the _servers directory_ and discover tablet servers. Chubby provides an efficient mechanism for tablet servers to check whether they still hold their lock without incurring network traffic. The master uses Chubby to detect when a tablet server is no longer serving its tablets and to reassign those tablets as soon as possible. Additionally, Chubby is used by the master to prevent concurrent master instantiations by grabbing a unique _master_ lock. 
    
    In more detail, as described in **5.2 Tablet Assignment (Pages 5-5)**, when a tablet server starts, it creates and acquires an exclusive lock on a uniquely-named file in a specific Chubby directory. If a tablet server loses its exclusive lock, it stops serving its tablets. The master monitors this directory to discover tablet servers and detects when a tablet server is no longer serving its tablets by periodically asking each tablet server for the status of its lock. 
    
    Overall, Chubby plays a crucial role in managing the assignment of tablets to tablet servers and ensuring the consistency and availability of the Bigtable system, as explained in **5.2 Tablet Assignment (Pages 5-5)**.
