    In this model, a table can store various aspects of data, such as web pages, with URLs as row keys and different aspects of the web pages as column names (**2 Data Model**, Pages 1-1). The contents of the web pages can be stored in a specific column, such as the "contents:" column, under the timestamps when they were fetched (**2 Data Model**, Pages 1-1). 
    
    For example, in a table called the "Webtable", the row name can be a reversed URL, the contents column family can contain the page contents, and the anchor column family can contain the text of any anchors that reference the page (**2 Data Model**, Pages 1-1). Each cell in the table can have multiple versions, with each version associated with a specific timestamp (**2 Data Model**, Pages 1-1).
