    Bigtable's data model is a "sparse, distributed, persistent multidimensional sorted map" (**2 Data Model**, Page 1). This map is indexed by three keys: a row key (string), a column key (string), and a timestamp (int64), with each corresponding value being an uninterpreted array of bytes. This is formally expressed as: `(row:string, column:string, time:int64) → string` (**2 Data Model**, Page 1).
    
    The provided example of a *Webtable* illustrates this model. Row keys are reversed URLs (e.g., "com.cnn.www"). Columns are grouped into "column families" such as "contents:" and "anchor:" (**2 Data Model**, Page 1). Within a row, a specific column (e.g., "anchor:cnnsi.com") can contain a cell with data. Each cell can have multiple versions indexed by timestamp, as shown by the contents column having three versions at timestamps t3, t5, and t6 (**2 Data Model**, Page 1).
    
