    The compression is applied per SSTable block within a locality group, not to the entire SSTable file. This allows small portions to be read without decompressing the entire file **[Compression (Pages 7-7)]**.
    
    The two-pass scheme is described as follows:
    1.  The first pass uses **Bentley and McIlroy's scheme**, which "compresses long common strings across a large window" **[Compression (Pages 7-7)]**.
    2.  The second pass uses **a fast compression algorithm** that "looks for repetitions in a small 16 KB window of the data" **[Compression (Pages 7-7)]**.
    
    The document notes that this two-pass scheme is chosen for speed but achieves high compression ratios (e.g., 10-to-1 for Webtable) because applications often cluster similar data via their row naming, allowing the Bentley-McIlroy algorithm to identify large amounts of shared content **[Compression (Pages 7-7)]**.
    
    Clients have control over whether compression is used and can specify the format, though the described two-pass scheme is what "many clients" use **[Compression (Pages 7-7)]**.
