    (row:string, column:string, time:int64) → string (****2 Data Model****, Pages 1-1).
    
    An example of how this data model is applied can be seen in a table designed to store web pages, referred to as the _Webtable_. In this table, URLs are used as row keys, various aspects of web pages are represented as column names, and the contents of the web pages are stored in a specific column under timestamps indicating when they were fetched (****2 Data Model****, Pages 1-1). 
    
