    An example of how this data model is applied can be seen in a table designed to store web pages, where URLs are used as row keys and various aspects of the web pages are represented as column names. The contents of the web pages are stored in a specific column under timestamps indicating when they were fetched (****2 Data Model****, Pages 1-1). 
    
    This structure allows for multiple versions of data to be stored, as illustrated by the example where the contents column has three versions at different timestamps (****2 Data Model****, Pages 1-1).
